# Cataloging Digital Geographic Data in the Information Infrastructure: A Literature and Technology Review.

**Authors:** Frank, Steven

## Abstract
Looks at some of the problems of finding digital geographic data in the electronic information infrastructure. Discusses the literature describing trends in organizing information resources in an electronic environment, including spatial information cataloging systems; the paper-based system from which they arose; and new Internet finding tools. (Contains 116 references.) (KRN)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ489685

